        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.047,
            0.419,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.088,
            0.846,
            0.129
          ],
          "content": "6. [Śulba-Sūtras] Give a method to obtain a rectangle of the same area as a given triangle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.136,
            0.846,
            0.177
          ],
          "content": "7. [Śulba-Sūtras] An isosceles triangle can be converted into a rectangle by dissection in a simpler way. Can you find out how to do it?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.411,
            0.191,
            0.582,
            0.335
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_16_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.349,
            0.846,
            0.406
          ],
          "content": "[**Hint:** Show that triangles ∆ADB and ∆ADC can be made into halves of a rectangle. Figure out how they should be assembled to get a rectangle. Use cut-outs if necessary.]"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.415,
            0.845,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": "8. [Śulba-Sūtras] Give a method to convert a rectangle into an isosceles triangle by dissection."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.463,
            0.847,
            0.54
          ],
          "content": "9. Which has greater area — an equilateral triangle or a square of the same sidelength as the triangle? Which has greater area — two identical equilateral triangles together or a square of the same sidelength as the triangle? Give reasons."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.558,
            0.273,
            0.579
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Rhombus"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.59,
            0.848,
            0.683
          ],
          "content": "Since a rhombus is a parallelogram, the area formula for a parallelogram holds for a rhombus as well. However, the additional properties of a rhombus give us another method to transform a rhombus into a rectangle of the same area by dissection. This method occurs in one of the Śulba-Sūtras."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.693,
            0.364,
            0.716
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "？ Try working this out!"
        },
        {
